{"id":"word:hebrew:H8334","type":"word","title":"שָׁרַת","subtitle":"H8334 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to attend as a menial or worshipper; figuratively, to contribute to","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁרַת (H8334) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 98 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁרַת (shârath) means to attend as a menial or worshipper; figuratively, to contribute to First listed occurrence: 1Chr 6 17."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁרַת","transliteration":"shârath","pronunciation":"shaw-rath'","strong":"H8334","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8334","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לְ/שָׁרֵ֣ת","לְ/שָׁרֵ֖ת","מְשָׁרֵ֥ת","לְ/שָׁ֣רְת֔/וֹ","מְשָׁרְתֵ֖י"],"morphs":[["HR/Vpc",18],["HVprmpc",9],["HVprmpa",8],["HVpi3mp",8],["HVprmpc/Sp3ms",7],["HR/Vpc/Sp3ms",6],["HTd/Vprmpa",6],["HVprmsc/Sp3ms",5],["HVprmsa",3],["HVprmsc",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to attend as a menial or worshipper; figuratively, to contribute to","usage":"minister (unto), (do) serve(-ant, -ice, -itor), wait on.","full":"H8334. sharath [ שָׁרַת ] 97 verb Pi`el minister, serve (compare Late Hebrew שֵׁרוּת (temple-) ministry , Phoenician משרת ministry , and perhaps verb שרת minister ); — Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular שֵׁרֵת Num 8:26 ; Deut 18:7 ; 3 masculine plural שֵׁרְתוּ Num 3:6 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular וַיְשָׁ֫רֶת Gen 39:4 , 3 masculine plural יְשָֽׁרְתוּ Num 3:31 +, etc.; Infinitive construct לְשָׁרֵת Exod 28:35 +, שָׁם לְשָׁ֫רֶת Deut 17:12 , etc.; Participle מְשָׁרֵת Num 11:28 + ( 2Sam 13:9 see מַשְׂרֵת , p. 602:a), feminine מְשָׁרַת 1Kin 1:15 , etc.; &#8212; serve: 1 of ministerial service (opposed tomenial, עבד ): a. higher domestic service: Joseph Gen 39:4 ; 40:4 (JE), Elisha's chief servant 2Kin 4:43 ; 6:15 , royal domestics 2Sam 13:17-18 , 1Kin 10:5 ; 2Chr 9:4 ; Est 2:2 ; 6:3 , Abishag 1Kin 1:4 , 15 . b. of royal officers (late) 1Chr 27:1 ; 28:1 ; 2Chr 17:19 ; 22:8 ; Est 1:10 ; Prov 29:12 . c. Joshua as chief assistant to Moses Exod 24:13 ; 33:11 (E), Num 11:28 (J), Josh 1:1 (D), Elisha to Elijah 1Kin 19:21 . d. of angels to ׳י Psa 103:21 , compare 104:4 . e. of kings of nations in prophets Isa 60:10 . 2 usually of special service in worship: a. of Levitical priests , absolute 1Kin 8:11 2Chr 5:14 ; with accusative ׳י Deut 10:8 ; 17:12 ; 21:5 ; Jer 33:21 +? אֹתִי מְשָֽׁרְתֵי 33:22 ; also Isa 60:7 of animals put figurative for those sacrificing them; of foreigners admitted to priesthood 61:6 , compare 56:6 ; so probably Samuel conceived as priest 1Sam 2:11 ; 3:1 , י פני ׳את 2:18 ( פני probably accusative, compare ᵐ5 τῷ προσώπῳ 2:11 ), ׳שׁ י ׳בְּשֵׁם Deut 18:5 , 7 . b. Levites (P, and late); with accusative of Aaronic priests Num 3:6 ; 8:26 ; 18:2 , with accusative of ׳י 1Chr 15:2 ; 2Chr 29:11 a; probably also in reference to Levitical singer Psa 101:6 ; with accusative tabernacle Num 1:50 (P), congregation 16:9 (P), people Ezek 44:11 + 44:12 (of idolatry); absolute 1Chr 16:4 ; 2Chr 23:6 ; 29:11 ; b 31:2 ; Ezra 8:17 (participle as substantive, ministers ); י בְּרִית ׳אֲרוֺן ׳שׁ לִפְנֵי 1Chr 16:37 , ׳שׁ הַכֹּהֲנִים נֶגֶד 2Chr 8:14 ; ׳שׁ with ב location 1Chr 26:12 ; especially with בְּ , of sacred vessels Num 3:31 ; 4:9 , 12 , 14 ; 2Kin 25:14 = Jer 52:18 ; בַּשִּׁיר 1Chr 6:17 . c. Zadokite priests (Ezekiel), absolute Ezek 42:14 3 t., with accusative ׳י 40:48 4 t., construct מְשָׁרֲתֵי before sacred place 45:4-5 , 46:24 . d. Aaronic priests, absolute Exod 28:35 4 t. P; with accusative ׳י 1Chr 23:13 ; ׳לי 2Chr 13:10 ; י ׳מְשָֽׁרְתֵי Joel 1:9 , 13 ; 2:17 , מזבח מְשָֽׁרְתֵי 1:13 , with בַּקֹּדֶשׁ Exod 28:43 4 t. P. e. of idolatry, with accusative ואבן עץ Ezek 20:32 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 6 17","keyReferences":["1Chr 6 17","1Chr 15 2","1Chr 16 4","1Chr 16 37","1Chr 23 13","1Chr 26 12","1Chr 27 1